[patterns/application/extensions/PTN-APP-EXT-007-entity-framework-extensibility-pattern.md#pattern-description]

### Pattern Description

This pattern provides three approaches for extending EF Core data models:

**Approach 1: Shadow Properties** (Recommended for simple extensions)

Add properties to entities without modifying entity classes using EF's shadow property feature:

```csharp
public class TexasClaimsExtensionContext : DbContext
{
    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
    {
        // Add shadow property to existing Claim entity
        modelBuilder.Entity<Claim>()
            .Property<string>("Ext_TexasTrackingNumber")
            .HasMaxLength(50);

        modelBuilder.Entity<Claim>()
            .Property<DateTime?>("Ext_TexasReceivedDate");

        // Index on shadow property
        modelBuilder.Entity<Claim>()
            .HasIndex("Ext_TexasTrackingNumber");
    }
}
```

**Access Pattern**:
```csharp
// Write
context.Entry(claim).Property("Ext_TexasTrackingNumber").CurrentValue = "TX-2024-001";
await context.SaveChangesAsync();

// Read
var trackingNumber = context.Entry(claim)
    .Property("Ext_TexasTrackingNumber").CurrentValue as string;

// Query
var claims = await context.Claims
    .Where(c => EF.Property<string>(c, "Ext_TexasTrackingNumber") == "TX-2024-001")
    .ToListAsync();
```

**Approach 2: Extension Tables with 1:1 Relationship** (For complex extensions)

Create separate extension tables linked to core entities:

```csharp
// Extension entity
public class CaliforniaClaimExtension
{
    public int ClaimId { get; set; } // FK to Claim
    public string CaliforniaAuthorizationCode { get; set; }
    public DateTime CaliforniaSubmissionDate { get; set; }
    public string CaliforniaProviderLicense { get; set; }

    // Navigation
    public Claim Claim { get; set; }
}

public class CaliforniaExtensionContext : DbContext
{
    public DbSet<CaliforniaClaimExtension> CaliforniaClaimExtensions { get; set; }

    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
    {
        modelBuilder.Entity<CaliforniaClaimExtension>()
            .HasKey(e => e.ClaimId);

        modelBuilder.Entity<CaliforniaClaimExtension>()
            .HasOne(e => e.Claim)
            .WithOne()
            .HasForeignKey<CaliforniaClaimExtension>(e => e.ClaimId);
    }
}
```

**Approach 3: Separate Extension DbContext** (For independent extension data)

Completely separate context for extension-only entities:

```csharp
public class FloridaReferenceData
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string CountyCode { get; set; }
    public string CountyName { get; set; }
    public List<string> ApprovedProviderTypes { get; set; }
}

public class FloridaExtensionContext : DbContext
{
    public DbSet<FloridaReferenceData> ReferenceData { get; set; }

    // Completely independent from product context
}
```

**Value Converters for Custom Types**:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Claim>()
    .Property(c => c.Metadata)
    .HasConversion(
        v => JsonSerializer.Serialize(v, (JsonSerializerOptions)null),
        v => JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, string>>(v, (JsonSerializerOptions)null));
```

